From 524f0ed1491c323d1b11059c3ff1d220f75dbd4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben <60955077+tencur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:26:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] napari_trainer: stop before saving when the split leaves
 no training patch

When the default train/validation split sends every selected patch to
validation (e.g. a single qualifying patch), the run now raises before the
trainer creates its checkpoint directories, instead of taking no optimizer
step and writing a final checkpoint over an earlier one. The check sits on
the trainer's own split (_configure_dataloaders), in a subclass used only by
the napari widget.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
