From 3c209902f37a0bc416c1fe4528f7df659b458359 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben <60955077+tencur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:28:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] napari_trainer: select patches without ignored voxels and
 train on exactly those

The widget now selects the training patches itself with find_valid_patches,
passing the first target's ignore label, so ignored voxels never count
toward Min Labeled Percentage and labels made only of the ignore value give
no patch. It writes the selection as the patch cache under the parameters
ZarrDataset looks it up with, and the trainer stops before saving anything
if its datasets do not read exactly the selected patches (e.g. after a cache
miss, which would enumerate every patch).

Rejected before anything is exported:
- targets with different valid_patch_value (the cache has one value; a null
  on one target and 2 on another made the dataset miss the cache);
- an image without a label layer for every target of the run (with
  allow_unlabeled_data the missing label became an all-zero target in the
  loss; without it the dataset raised FileNotFoundError mid-run);
- unlabeled_foreground_enabled, which adds patches nobody selected.

generate_patch_caches is restored to main's version: the napari trainer no
longer uses the generate_patch_caches_for_config split.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
