Subject: [PATCH 3/4] napari_trainer: keep configured losses and refuse losses
 that cannot take the labels

A target the selected config gives losses keeps them; the widget's loss now
only fills targets without configured losses. With the documented ink
(Dice + CE, two channels) and damage (BCEWithLogits, one channel) targets,
the widget no longer puts Dice + CE on damage, which failed on the first
batch with "IndexError: Target 1 is out of bounds".

Before anything is exported, a target is refused when its Dice + CE loss has
fewer than two output channels or label values outside 0..out_channels-1, or
its BCEWithLogits loss has more than one output channel or labels other than
0/1 (the ignore label excepted). Other configured losses are kept unchecked.

