From 56b28fcb8efb9f31fce9805ed2a6b48c84a7effd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben <60955077+tencur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:31:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] napari_trainer: infer with the checkpoint's preprocessing
 and on the source layer's grid

Normalization: a checkpoint that saved normalization_scheme and
intensity_properties (save_checkpoint stores the training dataset's) is now
normalized as the trainer's ZarrDataset normalized each patch: the
normalizer is built by ZarrDataset's own _initialize_normalization and
applied to each window's part inside the image, which is then zero-padded,
as ZarrDataset pads a patch. A zscore checkpoint now sees windows with mean
0 and standard deviation 1 instead of min-max values around 0.5. A
checkpoint without a saved scheme keeps the whole-image min-max scaling
unchanged.

Placement: each prediction layer gets the source layer's scale, translate,
rotate, shear and affine on its spatial axes (identity on the leading
batch and channel axes), so it overlays a rotated, scaled or translated
source.

The batch passed to the network is made contiguous.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
